e inside the allow-list succeeds', but the plan never states WHICH path(s) the allow-list contains. The venv is explicitly excluded; the included writable paths (presumably the git-archive temp source tree and mutmut's scratch) are left for the executor to derive.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22de268287dd3bb2","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1 and AC3","norm_id":"n905c8420ee924d03","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must pick which directory the 'write inside succeeds' probe targets and which paths the wrapper allows, without a stated default"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a line naming the allow-list members: the temp source-tree dir from `git archive` plus mutmut's scratch/working directory, with everything else (notably the venv/site-packages and $HOME) denied.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the '(allow default) + (deny file-write*)' Seatbelt posture against documented allow-default-Seatbelt escape prior art, or adopt a deny-default profile that allow-lists only what shard tests need.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: '(allow default) + (deny file-write*) + an allow-list subpath'","Retrieved: Pillar Security, 'Escaping Antigravity's Allow-Default Seatbelt' (pillar.security/blog/escaping-antigravitys-allow-default-seatbelt) documents an escape class against Seatbelt profiles that open with (allow default) then subtract dangerous operations","Retrieved: same source notes a sandbox-exec profile 'can only restrict... operations the process would otherwise be allowed to perform' — an allow-default base grants broad latitude a deny-default base would not","Threat model is a mutant that removed a deletion guard, i.e. adversarial-shaped code, which is the case allow-default profiles are weakest against"],"finding":"The plan adopts a Seatbelt '(allow default) + (deny file-write*)' profile without considering documented prior art on the weakness of allow-default (subtract-deny) Seatbelt profiles, against a threat model (adversarial mutant code) where that posture is precisely the class shown to be escapable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd40c2b985f9e8557","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanisms > macOS — Seatbelt; AC line 'macOS uses Seatbelt sandbox-exec with a generated profile'","norm_id":"nd6ea7a98ad3f9de0","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A mutant reaches an operation not covered by (deny file-write*) — e.g. a write via a path or mechanism the subtractive deny does not name — that a deny-default profile would have blocked by construction"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a short prior-art note citing the allow-default Seatbelt escape class and either (a) switch the generated profile to deny-default with an explicit allow-list, or (b) argue why (deny file-write*) is sufficient given the specific